; ==== the engine (T4): names and what the code shows
; Checked by running (tools/run.py) where it says so; the rest is read
; from the code. "Presumably" marks a guess.
; ---- start-up and the game states
; (not mapped) name CODE:0000 start
; (not mapped) comment CODE:0000 start: memory, the table number from the command line, mode 13h, INT 9, options, high scores
; (not mapped) name CODE:0089 main_loop
; (not mapped) comment CODE:0089 calls the routine of the game state [game_state] (state_table), for ever
name DATA:81BB state_table
name DATA:8A9B game_state
comment DATA:8A9B the game state, an index into state_table (checked: 1 at start, 2 idle, 3 ball start, 5 playing, 6 ball lost)
name DATA:972B table_num
comment DATA:972B the table, 0-3, the digit on the command line (checked)
; (not mapped) name CODE:4F39 st_quit
; (not mapped) comment CODE:4F39 state 0: saves the high scores, then state 10
name CODE:009E st_load
comment CODE:009E state 1: loads the table (files, set-up, lights, screen, palette) and the sound driver, then state 2
name CODE:00EA st_idle
comment CODE:00EA state 2: no game; the display and the table scroll up and down; F1-F8 start a game for 1-8 players, Esc asks to quit
name CODE:01BC game_scroll_down
comment CODE:01BC scrolls the table down to its end, then state 3 (also where a new game from the game over state goes on)
name CODE:04E5 st_ball_start
comment CODE:04E5 state 3: a new ball for the current player: the ball to the plunger, "player n" on the display for 46h frames, then plays until the ball leaves the plunger lane (x < [lane_exit_x]), then state 5
name CODE:04ED ball_start
name CODE:0552 ball_start_loop
name CODE:041E st_ball_locked
comment CODE:041E state 4: a ball was locked (lock_ball): a new ball to the plunger, the table scrolls down, then as state 3 (presumably; not seen running)
name CODE:0652 st_play
comment CODE:0652 state 5: the game: scroll, ball, nudge, plunger, the table's logic, drawing; ball drained: state 6; Esc: state 2
name CODE:15E3 st_ball_lost
comment CODE:15E3 state 6: the ball is lost: scrolls down, bonus (times the multiplier) and boosters counted into the score, then the next player (state 3), or a locked ball back into play (state 5), or game over (state 7)
name CODE:169E ball_lost_count
name CODE:1725 count_boosters
comment CODE:1725 the player's boosters ([+10h], BCD), each adds [booster_value] (10000) at the player's record +4 (by the display code that is past the six bytes of the score; not checked by running)
name CODE:1794 next_player
name CODE:17DD release_locked_ball
comment CODE:17DD a ball is locked: the first lock of td_locks puts its ball back into play (position and speed from the lock's object), state 5
name CODE:1872 st_game_over
comment CODE:1872 state 7: high score entry for each player, then the scores in turn; F1-F8 start a new game, else state 2
name CODE:1327 st_pause
comment CODE:1327 state 8 (key P): the music paused, "game paused"; Esc asks to quit, any other key goes on (state 5)
name CODE:12BC st_tilt
comment CODE:12BC state 9: tilt: flippers off, the ball's bonus cleared, "tilt" until the ball drains, then state 6
name CODE:1A23 st_exit
comment CODE:1A23 state 10: INT 9 back, palette black, video memory cleared, exit to DOS
name CODE:1A1C st_restart
comment CODE:1A1C states 11, 13-15: state 1 again
name CODE:4C24 st_12
comment CODE:4C24 state 12: player 1's score in a text, then state 11; nothing sets state 12 (left over, presumably)
; (not mapped) name CODE:0FA3 fatal_error
; (not mapped) comment CODE:0FA3 a file could not be loaded: sound off, text mode, the error text, exit
name CODE:4C81 parse_cmdline
comment CODE:4C81 BX = PSP: the first digit of the command line minus '0' into BL; CF when there is none
name CODE:0FBD print_at
comment CODE:0FBD not called: the DOS text at DS:DX ('$' at its end) at the cursor CX (column, row), the cursor read back after it
name CODE:0FCE set_cursor
comment CODE:0FCE the BIOS cursor to cursor_col/cursor_row on cursor_page
name CODE:0FDF get_cursor
name DATA:96ED cursor_col
name DATA:96EE cursor_row
name DATA:96EF cursor_page
name CODE:009B exit_jump
comment CODE:009B not reached: a jump to st_exit
name CODE:4CAE dos_alloc
comment CODE:4CAE AX paragraphs -> AX = segment (CF on failure)
name CODE:4CBB dos_free
name CODE:4CC6 dos_resize
comment CODE:4CC6 not called
; (not mapped) name CODE:4E23 load_file
; (not mapped) comment CODE:4E23 the file named at DS:DX into ES:DI, 32 KB at a time; CF on failure
name CODE:4DB6 load_options
comment CODE:4DB6 C:\DELUXE\DDPCOPTN.BIN into the options (9A96h), or the defaults when it is missing; opt_balls 1 becomes 3 balls, else 5
name CODE:276D load_hiscores
comment CODE:276D C:\DELUXE\HISCORES.PD1 into hiscores, or the defaults (hiscores_default) when it is missing
name CODE:274D save_hiscores
; (not mapped) name CODE:27AC write_file
; (not mapped) comment CODE:27AC creates the file DS:DX and writes [96E3h] bytes from DI (DS = AX)
; ---- the per-table set-up
name CODE:0690 load_table_files
comment CODE:0690 TBLDETLO.xxx (collision map, lower level) to BSS:0960, TBLDETHI.xxx (upper level, not for Ignition) to BSS:47E0, TABLE2M.xxx (the picture) to a new block ([table_pic_seg])
; (not mapped) name CODE:0710 table_setup
; (not mapped) comment CODE:0710 the ball, plunger and two unused object records, the table's own set-up, the flipper sprites' first frames
; (not mapped) name CODE:0788 setup_ignition
; (not mapped) comment CODE:0788 fills the table descriptor (8494h..84E0h) and the table's constants; the same for the other three
; (not mapped) name CODE:08EC setup_steel_wheel
; (not mapped) name CODE:0A50 setup_beat_box
; (not mapped) name CODE:0BBA setup_nightmare
name CODE:0D04 place_flipper_shapes
comment CODE:0D04 each shape record of flipper_shape_data: y := [flipper_y], x from the list at SI
name CODE:4B76 table_check
comment CODE:4B76 does nothing (called by each table's set-up; see machine_check)
name CODE:4B78 machine_check
comment CODE:4B78 not called: compares machine_checksum with the one stored at 8440h (a copy protection taken out, presumably)
name CODE:4BB9 machine_checksum
comment CODE:4BB9 a sum of the BIOS ROM, the free space of the current drive and the first hard disk's parameters (INT 41h vector)
name CODE:0E24 init_lights
comment CODE:0E24 gives each light record its palette slot (+22h) and copies the lights' "off" colours into light_palette
; (not mapped) name CODE:108F setup_screen
; (not mapped) comment CODE:108F the screen mode (opt_screen), the table picture into video memory, FLIPPERS.SPR loaded and made into sprite shapes, the split screen for the display
name CODE:0D2D new_game
comment CODE:0D2D clears the eight players' records and the jackpots; player 1; balls from the options; random seed from the frame counter
; ---- one frame of play
name CODE:021B read_game_keys
comment CODE:021B F1-F8: number of players - 1 into last_player; Esc: quit_request
name CODE:02A5 ask_quit
comment CODE:02A5 "really quit <y/n>": CF when Y
name CODE:02D6 idle_show
comment CODE:02D6 state 2's show: the texts of td_idle_texts, the table scrolling up and down (idle_scroll)
name CODE:0399 scroll_toward
comment CODE:0399 one scroll step toward the line [89BBh]/8
name CODE:03D7 idle_scroll
comment CODE:03D7 one scroll step down to the end, then up to the top ([89BDh] the direction)
name CODE:05BD show_player_up
comment CODE:05BD during the ball start: "player n" / the players and the ball number, blinking
name CODE:0FF0 reset_ball
comment CODE:0FF0 the ball to its start (ball_start_x/y), speed 0, gravity from opt_slope, flippers on, the table's objects for a new ball
name CODE:2804 reset_ball_objects
comment CODE:2804 the ball to its start, and the per-ball state: locks, bonus (unless held), multiplier 1, the event stack, the lower level's lists
name CODE:1153 ball_frame
comment CODE:1153 key P: state 8; three ball_step; the ball's position into its object and sprite; below line 512: ball_drained
name CODE:1222 nudge
comment CODE:1222 the nudge key shakes the table (nudge_phase, nudge_push); more than three nudges within 46h frames: tilt (state 9) (checked: the key; the tilt not)
name CODE:1376 plunger
comment CODE:1376 key held: plunger_pull counts to 20h, the plunger sprite moves down; let go: the ball in the lane gets a speed of -pull*80h (checked)
name CODE:140A scroll_follow
comment CODE:140A the scroll speed from the ball's height on the screen (a dead zone of 12h lines around line 37h)
name CODE:1456 scroll_step
comment CODE:1456 scroll += scroll_speed, kept within the table; the CRTC start address from it (nudge_phase shakes it by a line)
name CODE:15CC set_screen_start
comment CODE:15CC the CRTC start address [screen_start], then wait_frame
name CODE:14E8 play_frame
comment CODE:14E8 the table's logic for a frame: texts, timers, the hit rectangles and lanes, the map's events, the event stack, drawing, the groups of lights
name CODE:2BB1 lights_frame
comment CODE:2BB1 the lights for a frame: blinking, the current player's lights into the palette, Ignition's timers, the light chains
name CODE:2BC0 idle_lights
name CODE:158D copy_to_vram
comment CODE:158D CX bytes of a picture (4 planes interleaved, segment AX) into video memory at DI, plane by plane
; ---- keyboard
name CODE:2A94 hook_int9
name CODE:2AB9 unhook_int9
name CODE:2ACF kbd_int
comment CODE:2ACF INT 9: key_map bit n = scancode n down; E0-prefixed keys + 80h, the E0 shifts dropped (checked)
; (not mapped) name CODE:2B58 wait_keys_up
; (not mapped) comment CODE:2B58 until no key is down
name CODE:2B47 wait_key_down
comment CODE:2B47 until a key is down (not called)
name DATA:96CD key_map
comment DATA:96CD 256 bits: bit n = scancode n is down; tested as byte index + mask, the words of the options
name DATA:82BB old_int9
name CODE:2B2B kbd_e0
comment CODE:2B2B an E0 prefix came
; ---- the ball
name CODE:1EF1 ball_step
comment CODE:1EF1 one physics step (three a frame): the flippers swept against the ball, the ball moved through the collision map pixel by pixel (bounces), position += speed, then flippers and gravity
name CODE:1EA7 ball_step_size
comment CODE:1EA7 the step's pixels in x and y and their directions (977Eh..9781h)
name CODE:1BE3 ball_collide
comment CODE:1BE3 the ball's next pixel against the collision map (map_test) and the flippers' shapes; CF and the surface when it hits
name CODE:1B7E map_test
comment CODE:1B7E the collision map at x = CX, y = DX (rows run-length coded, indexed at BSS:0): AL = what is there, CF when something
name CODE:1A57 index_map
; (not mapped) comment CODE:1A68 the row index (512 rows, 4 bytes each) at BSS:0 for the map the far pointer at BX points to (lower_map or upper_map)
name CODE:1A7C map_run
name CODE:1DA2 map_special
comment CODE:1DA2 surfaces with a high nibble: event numbers (map_event) and the codes of map_code
name CODE:1DF1 map_code
comment CODE:1DF1 codes in the map: FCh gravity 10h, FBh gravity 9 (seen on Beat Box), FEh up to the upper level (its map and lists, the ball drawn in front), FDh back (read, not seen); other values are event numbers
name CODE:1E81 collision_response
comment CODE:1E81 the hit point into hit_x/hit_y, then the routine of response_table for the surface (all: bounce_response)
name CODE:2521 bounce_response
name CODE:20B8 bounce
comment CODE:20B8 the ball's speed reflected at the surface (angle [9777h]) with the surface's constants (surface_params), the flippers' and the nudge's push added
name CODE:239E surface_params
comment CODE:239E the five constants of the surface type from surface_table; kickers (10h, 20h) score; the flippers (types 1, 2) push with their angular speed times the distance from their pivot
name CODE:1E61 cosine
comment CODE:1E61 cosine = sine of AL+40h
name CODE:1E63 sine
comment CODE:1E63 AL = angle (80h = half a turn): the magnitude from the quarter-wave table at ES:DX (sine_table); the sign is left in CH (presumably; read, not checked)
name CODE:1E9F load_far
comment CODE:1E9F ES:BX := the far pointer at [BX]
name CODE:2295 mul_fix
comment CODE:2295 DX times the 24-bit factor at [BX] (signed), the high part into BX (presumably fixed point; read, not checked)
name CODE:2303 add_s16
comment CODE:2303 DX (CL its sign) += the signed word at [BX-1]; bounce adds the surface's speed (surface_vx/vy) and nudge_push to the ball's before the reflection and takes them off after it (quarter_sub_s16, sub_s16)
name CODE:230F quarter_sub_s16
comment CODE:230F DX := DX / 4 (at least 1 when DX was 1..3), then minus the signed word at [BX-1] (sub_s16)
name CODE:2324 sub_s16
name CODE:22D2 mul_u16
name CODE:22E3 mul_s16
name CODE:2330 clamp_speed
comment CODE:2330 DX (with CL as its sign) kept within -0C80h..0C80h
name CODE:2353 div_u
name CODE:238E div_s
name CODE:2460 flippers_gravity
comment CODE:2460 the flipper keys (unless flippers_off) move the flippers; the flipper sprites; gravity added to the speed; table_push decays
name CODE:24BD flipper_move
comment CODE:24BD BX = a flipper: pressed (ZF clear) speeds it up, released drops it back; angle and frame (0-10h) from the speed
name CODE:19E8 draw_flippers
comment CODE:19E8 the flipper sprites' frames from the flippers' frames
name CODE:1A34 index_flipper_shapes
comment CODE:1A34 the 17 shape pointers (flipper_shapes) into flipper_shape_data
name CODE:1A93 flipper_sweep
comment CODE:1A93 BX = a flipper's frame pair: steps the drawn frame toward the wanted one, testing the ball at each step
name CODE:1AB2 flipper_hit
name CODE:1AEA shape_test
name DATA:9772 ball_x
comment DATA:9772 the ball's centre: x and y, 24 bits each, pixels * 400h; speed: pixels * 400h per step (checked against the screen)
name DATA:9775 ball_y
name DATA:977A ball_vx
name DATA:977C ball_vy
name DATA:9773 ball_x_hi
name DATA:9776 ball_y_hi
name DATA:977B ball_vx_hi
name DATA:977D ball_vy_hi
name DATA:8CF2 ball_start_x
comment DATA:8CF2 where a new ball starts: dwords, pixels * 2000h (plus 7 pixels: the sprite's corner)
name DATA:8CF4 ball_start_x_hi
name DATA:8CF6 ball_start_y
name DATA:8CF8 ball_start_y_hi
name DATA:8D4D ball_obj
comment DATA:8D4D records of 26h bytes: +0 flags (1 = shown), +2 x, +6 y (dwords, pixels * 2000h), +12h, +16h the speed; the ball, the plunger (8D62h); 8CF0h and 8D16h are set up and never used
name DATA:8D73 plunger_obj
name DATA:8D01 unused_obj1
name DATA:8D27 unused_obj2
name DATA:9778 plunger_pull
name DATA:89D0 lane_exit_x
comment DATA:89D0 the ball has left the plunger lane when its sprite's x is below this
name DATA:975B gravity_x
name DATA:975D gravity
comment DATA:975D added to ball_vy every step: 9 + 2 * (opt_slope - 1); the map codes FCh/FBh set 10h/9
name DATA:9787 surface
comment DATA:9787 what the ball hit: low nibble the response (response_table) and surface_table's entry, high nibble 10h/20h kickers, 80h..: special
name DATA:9788 surface_angle
name DATA:9796 hit_x
name DATA:9798 hit_y
comment DATA:9796 where the ball hit (pixels): the hit rectangles and lanes are tested with it
name DATA:81DD response_table
name DATA:81ED surface_table
comment DATA:81ED per surface type five words, copied to surface_params_v
name DATA:972E surface_params_v
name DATA:823B kicker_score1
comment DATA:823B score records of the kicker surfaces (types 10h and 20h), as an object's (presumably)
name DATA:8246 kicker_score2
name DATA:975F map_flags
name DATA:9760 map_event
comment DATA:9760 an event number from the map (FFh: none), run by map_event_run
name DATA:9745 table_push
name DATA:9738 surface_vx
comment DATA:9738 the speed of the surface hit: 0, or a flipper's at the hit point (its angular speed times the distance from the pivot; surface_params)
name DATA:973A surface_vy
name DATA:9747 surface_type
comment DATA:9747 the surface as surface_params found it; 5: the hit rectangles are not tested (test_hit_rects)
name DATA:973C nudge_push
name DATA:9748 nudge_timer
name DATA:9749 nudge_count
name DATA:974A nudge_key_down
name DATA:9782 nudge_phase
comment DATA:9782 0 still, 1 shaken down, 2 back up (a line on the screen each)
name DATA:89CF tilted
name DATA:8AD0 ball_drained
name DATA:8AA9 ball_held
comment DATA:8AA9 not 0: the ball does not move (in a hole, or a lock)
name DATA:8AD1 flippers_off
name DATA:8251 flipper_shape_data
comment DATA:8251 far pointers: the flipper shapes, the collision maps of the lower and the upper level (BSS, from TBLDETLO/TBLDETHI), the sine table (TDATA)
name DATA:8255 lower_map
name DATA:8259 upper_map
name DATA:825D sine_table
; (not mapped: DATA:8261 would be flipper_x and ign_flipper_x and flipper_x) name DATA:822E ign_flipper_x
