; (not mapped) comment CODE:27D5 not reached: sixteen INC AX in front of reset_targets
name CODE:2B7C clear_hit
comment CODE:2B7C hit_score, hit_object, hit_x/hit_y and hit_lane cleared, unless the ball is held
name CODE:32F6 pick_random_light
name CODE:3322 random_light_check
name CODE:4316 table_ball_events
comment CODE:4316 per table at a new ball (Steel Wheel, Nightmare: an event)
name CODE:4353 table_game_objects
; object handlers (+16h of an object; coderanges 3C4D-3F99, 4162-41B2)
name CODE:3C2E extra_ball_award
name CODE:3BC1 advance_object
comment CODE:3BC1 a handler (2Eh-byte objects): the sequence +28h one step on for the player (not onto a negative word), the first lamp not lit of the light group +2Ah lit (not with flag 8), the Ignition timer +2Ch restarted (+0 := +2)
name CODE:3C3B obj_nop1
comment CODE:3C3B handlers that do nothing (obj_nop1..6)
name CODE:3C3C obj_nop2
name CODE:3C3D obj_nop3
name CODE:3C3E obj_nop4
name CODE:3D66 obj_nop5
name CODE:3D67 obj_nop6
name CODE:3C3F lock_jackpot
comment CODE:3C3F the jackpot to the score, once more for each of the first two locks that is full (as meant), the count ("n x") into td_txt_jackpot4, the jackpot back to jackpot_base, the locks emptied
comment CODE:3C3F the test of a lock reads [BX+974Eh] (974Eh happens to be map_flags' address; kept a number) where [BX+4] (the lock's state) must have been meant (a bug, presumably): only Nightmare's objects use this handler, and there the first test reads BSS:44CCh, a byte of TBLDETLO.NTM (9Dh: always counted), the second one BSS:44D2h, past the end of that file (memory not loaded; not checked what it holds)
